{"pageProps":{"note":{"id":"qsxjfqd40qmv9pxbfqjr54l","title":"High Performance Networking","desc":"","updated":1736092233069,"created":1736088601948,"custom":{},"fname":"tech.high-performance-networking","type":"note","vault":{"name":"main","fsPath":"main","useFMTitle":false},"contentHash":"510e2d977cdfec97efcf2e4b24c89bc1","links":[],"anchors":{"high-performance-networking":{"type":"header","text":"High Performance Networking","value":"high-performance-networking","line":8,"column":0,"depth":1},"switches":{"type":"header","text":"Switches","value":"switches","line":17,"column":0,"depth":2}},"children":[],"parent":"fb9e4130-eaf8-425d-9039-5bc2ee876f18","data":{}},"body":"<h1 id=\"high-performance-networking\">High Performance Networking<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#high-performance-networking\"></a></h1>\n<p>At speeds beyond 10GBE, the CPU overhead of processing packets so quickly adds up.</p>\n<p>Hence, higher end NICs have offloads like RDMA which allows applications direct access to the NIC without going through the CPU.\nSome guides on enabling this:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://forum.level1techs.com/t/100-gbe-truenas-scale-23-10-iscsi-performance-unleashed/206452\">100 Gbe &#x26; TrueNAS Scale 23.10 iSCSI - Performance Unleashed</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"switches\">Switches<a aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"anchor-heading icon-link\" href=\"#switches\"></a></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://help.mikrotik.com/docs/spaces/ROS/pages/189497483/Quality+of+Service#QualityofService-RDMAoverConvergedEthernet%28RoCE%29\">Mikrotik supports ROCe in their switches</a>] as of RouterOS 7.17, <a href=\"https://forum.mikrotik.com/viewtopic.php?t=187501\">forum thread</a>. This is still in beta.</li>\n</ul>","noteIndex":{"id":"root","title":"root","desc":"","updated":1622102326440,"created":1595961348801,"custom":{"stub":false,"nav_order":0,"permalink":"/"},"fname":"root","type":"note","vault":{"name":"main","fsPath":"main","useFMTitle":fal